  clock: 3  # 1c43
  nonce: 1c43  # 1c43
  set:  # 1c43
    description: "Surfaced by an adversarial review of PR #4255 (emission-parity F4 / A2; cross-ref WI-dutov done, WI-jubag).\n\njs_ts.py _extract_inheritance_edges (def ~2771) processes only sym.kind=='class' (early 'if sym.kind != \"class\": continue', ~2834), and interface symbols are created WITHOUT any base_classes meta: the interface_declaration branch (~4422) builds the Symbol with no meta, and _extract_base_classes (~3817) is called only from the class branch (~4384). Consequently 'interface Child extends Base' produces ZERO inheritance edges whether Base is external or intra-repo.\n\nREPRO (analyzer): 'export interface Base {} ; export interface Child extends Base {}' -> no extends/implements edges; 'import { Observer } from \"rxjs\"; export interface MyObs extends Observer {}' -> no edges (should be 'extends typescript:rxjs:0-0:Observer:unresolved'). Interface nodes carry meta.base_classes = None.\n\nCross-language consumer expectation is established: the Java analyzer already extracts interface-extends (java.py ~1488, extends_interfaces) and emits through the shared core inheritance-linker (which accepts every kind in type_like_kind_names(), interface included).\n\nMINIMAL FIX: (1) extract interface bases into base_classes meta on interface symbols (handle the interface_declaration extends_type_clause, analogous to Java's extends_interfaces). Once interface symbols carry base_classes meta, the shared core inheritance.py linker emits intra-repo edges, AND its WI-jubag Approach C fallback (_external_base_edge, inheritance.py ~290) emits the external case as 'typescript:external:0-0:Observer:unresolved', with no further js_ts change. (2) Only the module hint ('typescript:rxjs:...' instead of 'typescript:external:...') still needs js_ts's own A2-style external fallback to cover interfaces (currently gated by kind!='class').\n\nEDGE TYPE: TS interfaces use 'extends' (not 'implements') for their bases, so an interface->interface edge must be 'extends'. The core resolve loop (inheritance.py ~474) tries the interface map first and labels ANY interface target 'implements', so step (1) alone would emit Child -implements-> Base. The fix must emit 'extends' for an interface source (in js_ts, or a source-kind check in core).\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 1c43
- op: discuss  # 8a3f
  at: '2026-10-01T07:30:44Z'  # 8a3f
  by: agent  # 8a3f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8a3f
  clock: 4  # 8a3f
  nonce: 8a3f  # 8a3f
  message: "IMPLEMENTED on local branch jgstern-agent/fix/kalug-ts-interface-extends (worktree ~/hg_wt/kalug), NOT pushed, status unchanged. Commits 03fc3823ba + 86058ca093.\n\njs_ts.py: _extract_interface_bases reads the interface extends_type_clause into meta.base_classes; _heritage_type_names is the one reader for a heritage TYPE list (interface extends + class implements) and adds nested_type_identifier, so `implements ng.OnInit` is no longer dropped either. _extract_inheritance_edges now handles interface sources: every edge from an interface is `extends` (to an interface, a class, or an unresolved external carrying its import module hint).\n\nCore linkers/inheritance.py: an inherently-abstract source (abstract_type_kind_names(): interface/trait/protocol) gets `extends` to an interface target (was `implements` regardless of source). This changes Java/PHP/Scala/Swift too: measured on fixtures, IChild/PChild/SChild/WChild -implements-> base BEFORE, -extends-> AFTER; class->interface unchanged. test_trait_extends_trait pinned `implements`; now pins `extends`. The analyzer-edge dedup is keyed on the (src,dst) pair, not (src,dst,type). Kotlin's own emitter labelled interface->interface `implements` and is fixed to `extends` (without that the pipeline would have carried both labels).\n\nLive repro after (survey of a fixture, worktree code): Child -extends-> Base (origin javascript, one edge); MyObs -extends-> typescript:rxjs:0-0:Observer (analyzer hint kept, no external twin); WidgetLike -extends-> Widget (class); K -implements-> Child; KChild -extends-> KBase (kotlin, one edge). Before (dev): zero edges for any TS interface source.\n\nTargeted smart-test (slot, 425 affected files): 14271 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed; changed source files at 100% coverage.\n\nResiduals filed: WI-ruzid-zuzod-zilup-hibub-zagod-lidav-ludan-badis (C# interface bases), WI-gutas-jufaz-puhoh-riram-zagid-hadal-gikap-pazim (Go interface embedding), WI-davih-bosov-fodar-kafon-tufoz-fodol-rugoh-purok (core mints `external` for a relative-import base js_ts drops; observed on FromLocal).\nNOT measured: any corpus repo (fixtures only), so no edge-count delta on real code is claimed."  # 8a3f
